# This directory holds sources only: the .hdoc documents, the CSL-JSON
# bibliography they name, and the figure they include. Anything else here is
# something a build produced.
#
# So: a whitelist, not a list of artifact extensions (TASK-50.5). The
# extension-list version had to be patched reactively twice -- once for the
# pdflatex byproducts, once for the .bib that native mode began generating in
# TASK-42 -- and both times the new artifact was noticed only by reading
# `git status --short` after it had already been committed. A whitelist cannot
# lag behind an artifact type nobody has seen yet.
#
# Two consequences worth knowing before adding anything here:
#
#   - subdirectories are ignored wholesale, which is what makes the recommended
#     `examples/out/` build directory (see the README's "Example" section)
#     invisible to git. A source subdirectory would need its own `!` rule.
#   - a source of a NEW type -- say a .csv a future example reads -- is ignored
#     until it is named below. `git add examples/data.csv` says so out loud;
#     `git add -A` just skips it.
#
# The figure is whitelisted by name, not as `*.png`: the one image type this
# directory actually generates is a rendered page (pdftoppm in TASK-29's
# review, --screenshot in TASK-43's), and `!*.png` would let those straight
# back in.
*
!.gitignore
!*.hdoc
!*.json
!catkins.png
